    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the question is the 5.00 SGD no-show fee on TRP-05069, charged to the rider at 13:33:44 on 2026-09-17 and then reversed to the rider and recovered from the driver (fee_reversed, 15:25:40). The driver filed, so the ruling states his outcome.\n\nThe fee was properly raised on this record. The driver's auto-arrival at Block 216 is recorded at 13:27:15 (EV-TRIP-05069) and is corroborated by the driver-device GPS trace (EV-GPS-05069, nearest fix index 12 at 13:27:10, 0.5 m from the pickup, 6 m reported accuracy, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and the 25 m accuracy filter). The trip was on-demand with no scheduled time, so under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait ran from arrival: it started 13:27:20 and expired 13:32:20, and the driver cancelled at 13:33:40, 385 seconds after arrival and after the wait had closed.\n\nTo the rider: your account that the driver never called and only messaged does not defeat the fee. POL-NS-23 requires at least one in-app chat message and at least one placed in-app call before cancellation, and it reads the call from trip_record.in_app_calls or a voice-call entry in the chat log. EV-CHAT-05069 carries two driver messages (13:27:40 and 13:32:00) and a voice-call entry at 13:30:15 recording an outgoing in-app call to you that rang 24 seconds, all before the 13:33:40 cancellation. The clause's test is the log, not recollection, and it requires the call to have been placed, not answered; the empty structured in_app_calls array does not matter because the clause expressly accepts the chat-log voice-call entry as the alternative. The contact obligation is therefore met and the fee is not voidable under POL-NS-23.\n\nOn the escalation you argued: POL-GEN-26 does not apply. The facts its rules need are carried by complete, unimpaired artifacts (trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown all at weight 1.0), so nothing is unestablishable and there is no open question for a human reviewer.\n\nTo the driver: the freight is exactly the 5.00 SGD POL-NS-22 fixes (EV-FARE-05069, fee_charged_sgd 5.00, policy_fee_sgd 5.00, fee_matches_policy true), so the fee stands and no fee-amount referral arises. You are owed the whole amount back: because the present state has the 5.00 SGD with the rider and recovered from you, the ruling moves it to you as DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD. No POL-NS-24 goodwill credit arises (you arrived and made contact), and the POL-NS-25 repeat counter is absent from the record, so there is no referral. With the amount below 10.00 SGD and fraud_flags of 0 on both profiles, POL-GEN-22 leaves the ruling final."
  },
